# CABLE FRONT KICK

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Cable Front Kick is an explosive resistance exercise designed to develop linear kicking power, hip extension, trunk stability and force transmission through the lower kinetic chain.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer resistance exercises for improving front kick performance across striking-based combat sports.

---

# Philosophy

A powerful front kick is not produced by the leg alone.

Force begins with the supporting foot, travels through the lower limb, hips and trunk, and is finally expressed through the striking leg.

The Cable Front Kick overloads this kinetic chain while maintaining sport-specific movement mechanics.

CAS uses the Cable Front Kick to increase kicking power while preserving technical precision.

